R["«O73»"] = """**(c)** Ranking quality on the test weeks: **OLS on log value is best on Spearman (0.469)**, then GBM on log value (0.461), hurdle GBM (0.456), multi-task MLP (0.452) and GBM on raw value (0.426). The segment-mean model (0.228) and the vendor-like 30-day model (0.241) are far behind. On top-decile capture and normalised Gini the **hurdle GBM is best** (31.7% and 0.584) against 29.7% and 0.545 for OLS, while the oracle ceiling for capture is 57.8%, so even the best model captures only about half of what is possible. Strict decile hits are only 12% to 16% (ceiling 68.5%), and within one decile 33% to 41% (ceiling 83.4%). **MAE misleads**: the OLS model has the best ranking but an MAE of ₹9,709, far worse than the constant-mean predictor (₹1,807), because a few huge back-transformed predictions dominate; the MLP has the lowest MAE (₹1,424). Choosing by MAE would pick a different model from choosing by ranking."""
